{"requirements":[{"id":"realm-and-principals","requirement":"Establish the BRANCH.TEST Kerberos realm on node1 with analyst and reports/node2.branch.test principals.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 directly shows the BRANCH.TEST database, both requested principals, an enabled and active KDC listening on TCP/UDP 88, and the same realm data recovered after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9cff8830d60f4a6e","cmd-338efc6bfe774772","cmd-57b787f68c9c4105","cmd-539f911688bc4a72"]},{"id":"ticket-and-keytab","requirement":"Provide the application keytab on node2, allow analyst to obtain the requested service ticket, and validate that ticket with the application keytab.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has a root-owned mode-0600 keytab containing the service principal. A fresh post-reboot analyst cache contains the requested service ticket, and node2 validates it against that keytab at kvno 2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8b75d9c2f9c64154","cmd-c7ed5923432445fa","cmd-3d23ac1af5ef4834","cmd-f4584875fefd4092","cmd-dbcbf05f0c9d44b5"]},{"id":"ownership-notes","requirement":"Keep the principal ownership notes under /srv/legacy2/kerberos-service-identity intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"On both nodes, final file hashes, ownership, permissions, and directory contents match the prepared baseline, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-f33f57014df44181","cmd-b23064bb230f4eb0","cmd-57b787f68c9c4105","cmd-bde0f351bbf94785","cmd-539f911688bc4a72","cmd-dbcbf05f0c9d44b5"]},{"id":"platform-compatibility","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor installed signed RHEL-native Kerberos 1.21.3 packages. Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution and reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4c09704f51ff44be","cmd-5fa9bdd1f4184e4f","cmd-539f911688bc4a72","cmd-dbcbf05f0c9d44b5","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.99,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, Kerberos configuration, realm and credential creation, firewall activation, and node reboots all served the task or mandatory restart protocol. Temporary ticket caches, staging keytabs, transfer private keys, known-host files, and two temporary SSH authorization entries were removed; final audits show no failed services or task-related /tmp residue. The unsuccessful OpenSSL attempt only created a secrets directory subsequently used by the successful implementation. Root-only rollback copies created before configuration changes had a clear safety role, although their eventual retention was not audited.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4c09704f51ff44be","cmd-5fa9bdd1f4184e4f","cmd-2d134fbe44894588","cmd-60fb7016bcde4936","cmd-8b75d9c2f9c64154","cmd-acd2d618ff3d4e97","cmd-602b983dd94643e0","cmd-3d23ac1af5ef4834","cmd-539f911688bc4a72","cmd-dbcbf05f0c9d44b5","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete on both nodes: healthy pre-restart states and boot IDs were captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, boot IDs changed, and the KDC, principals, application keytab, ticket flow, protected notes, and platform recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector inventories /tmp but not the root-only rollback directories created on each node, so their final retention or removal is not independently established.","There is no separate application daemon on node2 in scope; validation is demonstrated directly with Kerberos client commands and the deployed application keytab."]}
